sequenceDiagram
    participant P as pointer/touch (OSK, terminal mode)
    participant DR as KeyboardDriver (ferrokey-core)
    participant ST as KeyboardState
    participant RT as InputRouter (input.rs)
    participant TKS as TerminalKeySink (ferrokey-terminal)
    participant ENC as TerminalKeyEncoder
    participant PS as PtySink
    participant PTY as PTY master
    participant CH as child (shell / vim / htop / tmux)

    P->>DR: KeyAction::Down / Tap / Up
    DR->>ST: press(key, now)
    ST-->>DR: Vec<KeyEvent>
    DR->>RT: key_down / key_up
    RT->>TKS: (Destination::Terminal)
    TKS->>ENC: PhysicalKey + layout + modes
    ENC-->>PS: exact PTY bytes (bounded)
    PS->>PTY: write
    PTY->>CH: bytes to child stdin
    CH-->>PTY: output bytes
    PTY-->>PARSER: grid / scrollback update
